    "description": "Rion Co., Ltd. develops, manufactures, sells, and services particle counters, medical equipment, and environmental equipment in Japan. The company's audiological equipment includes hearing instruments, such as maxience, premience, wireless, Precia II / Precia IIV, classe series, high power series II, and trimmer type digital hearing aid; analog and digital BTE, trimmer digital BTE, in-the-ear ready and custom-made, and analog body aid instruments; and medical equipment comprising audiometers, impedance audiometer, and eustachian tube function meter. Its sound and vibration measuring instruments include sound level meters, vibration meters, seismometers, frequency analyzers, microphones and accelerometers, and other products. The company's particle counters comprise air and liquid-borne particle counters, and viable particle counters. Its products are primarily used in the applications of environment-related administration, electronics, semiconductors, pharmaceutical, and food manufacturing industries. The company was formerly known as Kobayashi-Riken Seisakusho Ltd. and changed its name to Rion Co., Ltd. in 1960. Rion Co., Ltd. was incorporated in 1944 and is headquartered in Kokubunji, Japan."
